how to write a good issue in github  github is a main place for the yogin  face open source library and you should  always go there to report a bug or ask  for a new feature  for more general questions or to debug  your own code use the forums see the  video link below  it's very important to write good issues  as it will help the bug you uncovered  bifix in no time  for this video we've created a version  of transformers with a back  you can install it by executing this  command in a notebook remove the  exclamation mark to execute it in a  terminal  in this version the following example  fails  the error is rather cryptic and does not  seem to come from anything in our code  so it seems we have a back to report  the first thing to do in this case is to  try to find the smallest amount of code  possible that reproduces the work  in our case inspecting the traceback  we see the failure happens inside the  pipeline function when it calls  autotokenizer.form retrained  using the debugger we find the values  passed to that method and can thus  create a small sample of code that  hopefully generates the same error  it's very important to go through this  step as you may realize there are always  on your side and not a bug in the  library but it also will make it easier  for the maintainers to fix your problem  here we can play around a bit more with  code and the t0 happens for different  checkpoints and not just this one and  that it disappears when we use useful  sequel force inside our tokenizer call  the important part is to have something  that does not depend on any external  files or data  try to replace your data by fake values  if you can't share it  with all of this done we are ready to  start writing our issue  click on the button next to bug report  and you will discover that there is a  template to fill it should only take you  a couple of minutes  the first thing is to properly name your  issue don't pick a title that is too  vague  then you have to fill your environment  information  for the command provided by the  transformers library to do this  just execute it in your notebook or in  the terminal and copy paste the results  there are two last questions to fill  manually to which the answers are no and  no in our case  next we need to determine where to tag  there is a full list of usernames in the  template since our issue has to do with  tokenizers we pick the maintainer  associated with them  there is no point tagging more than  three people they will redirect you to  the right person if you made a mistake  next we have to give the information  necessary to reproduce the bug  we based our sample and put it between  two lines with three back six  so that is formatted properly  we also paste the full trace back still  between two lines of three backticks  lastly  we can add any additional information  about what we tried to debug the issue  at hand  with all of this you should expect an  answer to your issue pretty fast and  hopefully a quick fix  note that all the advice into this video  applies for almost every open source  project
 

